      "spam": false,
      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "People often think its CPU heavy, it kinda is. But isn't at the same time. \nI never hit above 70% usage (in total including all the other software I run) on my CPU, due to the fact my GPU is running at 98% and hits a bottle neck there.\nVRChat just isn't a optimised game but for the most part its not VRChat's fault, its the content people make for it. \nMonitor your total utilisation on all your parts, I'm sure you'd see something running near max.\nAnd as a note Im running a i9-9900k clocked at 5.1GHz on all cores and a 2080ti yet I still get bad performance a lot.",
      "viewerReactions": null
    }
  ],
  "companyID": "58c62e995865713647a7115d",
  "created": "2020-07-28T09:43:07.160Z",
  "deletedAt": null,
  "details": "Other VR games take up about 40%-60% of my CPU, allowing them  the run smoothly. VRChat on the other hand is stuck at 20 and does not go over. Allowing the game to use more CPU would definitely let it run better, as it's still a terribly optimised game.",
